.TH LD 1 "November 2026" "ix"
.SH NAME
LD \- load English source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B LD
.I program
.RI [ request ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LD reads a prose program and asks its runner for one POSIX shell script.
On success the script appears on standard output. A program can use
.B #!/bin/LD
on ix, or
.B #!/usr/bin/env LD
on a system that installs LD in its search path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B LD_RUNNER
selects the runner. The default is
.BR lordhavemercy .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
LD NSH > nsh.new && sh -n nsh.new
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lord (1),
.BR nsh (1)
